    exampleHands: [
      'Setup example: 5 card(s) per player.',
      'Rule example: Be the first player or team to reach exactly 61 points by making the open ends of the layout total multiples of 3 or 5 (and optionally scoring for chipping out).',
      'Turn-flow example: First hand starter is determined by lot (e.g. each draws a tile, highest starts); in later hands the turn to start passes left. Play is clockwise. Each turn a player adds one tile to an end of the layout, matching the inward end of the played tile to the outward end of the tile it touches; doubles are placed crosswise and count as the total of their pips when at an open end. A player who cannot play must knock and the turn passes. The hand ends when one player chips out (plays their last tile) or all players are blocked; in the four-player partnership game both members of one team must chip out. After each play the two open ends are totalled: if the total is a multiple of 5, 3 or both, the player scores immediately (e.g. 3→1, 5→1, 6→2, 9→3, 10→2, 12→4, 15→8, 18→6, 20→4). Chip-out scores 1 point. First to exactly 61 wins; a score that would exceed 61 is disregarded.',
      'Scoring example: After each play, total the two open ends of the layout; if the total is a multiple of 5, 3 or both, score immediately (3→1, 5→1, 6→2, 9→3, 10→2, 12→4, 15→8, 18→6, 20→4). Chip-out scores 1. First to exactly 61 wins; scores that would exceed 61 are disregarded. First player or team to reach exactly 61 points wins..',
